[
  {
    "id": "c001",
    "name": "Preamble — Parties and Agreement",
    "text": "This AMENDED AND RESTATED SETTLEMENT, AMENDMENT, AND RELEASE AGREEMENT (this “Agreement”) dated as of May 19, 2016, is entered into by and among Aéropostale, Inc., Aéropostale Procurement Company, Inc. and their affiliated chapter 11 debtors 1 and debtors in possession (the “Debtors”) , and MGF Sourcing US, LLC (f/k/a TSAM (Delaware) LLC) (“MGF”)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c002",
    "name": "Preamble — Prior Agreement Superseded",
    "text": "This Agreement amends, restates and supersedes in its entirety that certain Settlement, Amendment, and Release Agreement dated as of May 16, 2016 among the undersigned parties."
  },
  {
    "id": "c003",
    "name": "Recital — Sourcing Agreement Definition",
    "text": "WHEREAS Aéropostale, Inc., Aéropostale Procurement Company, Inc. and MGF are each party to that certain Sourcing Agreement dated as of May 23, 2014 (as amended through the date hereof, the “Sourcing Agreement”);"
  },
  {
    "id": "c004",
    "name": "Recital — Bankruptcy Court Definition",
    "text": "WHEREAS the Debtors filed voluntary petitions for relief under chapter 11 of title 11 of the United States Code on May 4, 2016, in jointly administered cases captioned In re Aéropostale, Inc., et al., Case No. 16-11275 (SHL) pending before the United States Bankruptcy Court for the Southern District of New York (the “Bankruptcy Court);"
  },
  {
    "id": "c005",
    "name": "1(a) Delivery of Goods",
    "text": "1. Deliveries and Delivery Dates. (a) MGF shall deliver the goods identified on the Detailed Delivery Schedule (the “Goods”) in compliance with the delivery schedule set forth in the Detailed Delivery Schedule, or earlier as described below."
  },
  {
    "id": "c006",
    "name": "1(a) Detailed Delivery Schedule Definition",
    "text": "“Detailed Delivery Schedule” means the summary sheet and excel support provided to the Debtors by MGF on May 9, 2016, which is attached hereto as Exhibit A."
  },
  {
    "id": "c007",
    "name": "1(a) Goods Categories",
    "text": "For purposes of this Agreement, the terms “Open Commitments,” “Open CPOs”, “Open Orders”, “US Released for Delivery” and “Orders in Transit” are references to categories of Goods as identified on the Detailed Delivery Schedule."
  },
  {
    "id": "c008",
    "name": "1(b) Accelerated Deliveries",
    "text": "(b) MGF shall accelerate deliveries of Goods (or change shipping method from ocean freight to another method designated by the Debtors) where possible at the Debtors’ written election and at Debtors’ sole cost and sole risk of any delivery delays occasioned as result thereof (it being agreed that any re-direction of Goods from Debtors’ Canadian warehouse to the United States warehouses of the Debtors shall also be at Debtors’ sole cost and sole risk of any delivery 1 The Debtors are as follows: Aéropostale, Inc. (3880); Aéropostale West, Inc. (7013); Jimmy’Z Surf Co., LLC (0461); Aero GC Management LLC (4257); Aeropostale Procurement Company, Inc. (8518); Aeropostale Licensing, Inc. (8124); P.S. from Aeropostale, Inc. (5900); GoJane LLC (4923); Aeropostale Canada Corp. (N/A); Aeropostale Holdings, Inc. (7729); and Aeropostale Puerto Rico, Inc. (6477). The Debtors’ corporate headquarters is located at 112 West 34th Street, 22nd Floor, New York, NY 10120. 0652/21798-046 current/56348982v1 WEIL:\\95715512\\8\\11727.0013 16-11275-shl Doc 168 Filed 05/20/16 Entered 05/20/16 13:24:46 Main Document Pg 5 of 24 EXECUTION COPY delays occasioned as a result thereof). The parties"
  },
  {
    "id": "c009",
    "name": "1(b) NDC Assumption",
    "text": "The parties hereto each acknowledge that all “NDCs” listed on excel support portion of the Detailed Delivery Schedule (the “Excel Support”) assume ocean freight."
  },
  {
    "id": "c010",
    "name": "1(c) Payment and Discount",
    "text": "(c) The Debtors shall be obligated to pay for all Goods that are delivered at full contract price in the amount set forth in the Detailed Delivery Schedule on the terms set forth in section 3, subject to an 8.00% discount on all Open CPOs and Open Commitments, to be applied on a pro rata basis to payments for the Goods from the first delivery to the last delivery contemplated by this Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c011",
    "name": "1(c) Discount Exclusions",
    "text": "The parties hereto each acknowledge and agree that the foregoing discount does not apply for Goods in “US Released for Delivery” or “Orders in Transit” status on the Detailed Delivery Schedule (it being agreed that all Goods included in the “US Released for Delivery” and “Orders in Transit” categories and delivered to Debtors will be paid for by the Debtors at the full contract prices therefor set forth in the Excel Support)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c012",
    "name": "1(d) International Licensee Orders",
    "text": "(d) MGF shall front load the production and deliveries of open orders for the Debtors’ international licensees to the extent practicable."
  },
  {
    "id": "c013",
    "name": "1(d) International Licensee Discount",
    "text": "Subject to compliance by the Debtors’ international licensees with the terms of their orders (i.e., such licensees shall accept delivery of all orders and their account balances shall remain current), MGF shall provide a 10% discount on the international licensees’ orders if such orders are not ready for pick up by the applicable licensee at origin on the original FOB turnover date (subject to minor ordinary course delays of less than two weeks consistent with past practice)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c014",
    "name": "2. Inventory — Acceptance of Goods",
    "text": "2. Inventory. The Debtors shall take delivery of all Goods with no reductions and no cherry-picking (subject to the provisions of the Sourcing Agreement that provide for adjustments for defective product and similar adjustments, including without limitation nonconforming deliveries, excluding any right to reject late deliveries as non-conforming deliveries unless any such late delivery is ten (10) days or more past the scheduled delivery date set forth on the Detailed Delivery Schedule)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c015",
    "name": "2. Inventory — Early Deliveries",
    "text": "If MGF attempts delivery of Goods from Open Orders earlier than indicated on the Excel Support, the Debtors shall accept delivery of such Goods when delivery is attempted by MGF."
  },
  {
    "id": "c016",
    "name": "3. Trade Terms — Payment Timing",
    "text": "3. Trade Terms. The Debtors shall pay for the Goods delivered by MGF in full no later than fourteen (14) calendar days after delivery; provided that the Debtors shall pay for Goods to be delivered by MGF in full on a cash in advance basis (with respect to each specific individual delivery of Goods, no later than two business days prior to the delivery of any such Goods) after an Event of Default (as defined in the DIP Financing) has occurred under the Debtors’ current Secured Superpriority Debtor in Possession Loan, Security and Guaranty Agreement, the Interim Order Pursuant to 11 U.S.C. §§105, 361, 362, 363 and 364 and Rules 2002, 4001 and 9014 of the Federal Rules of Bankruptcy Procedure (i) Authorizing Incurrence by the Debtors of Postpetition Secured Indebtedness, (ii) Granting Liens, (iii) Authorizing Use of Cash Collateral by the Debtors and Providing for Adequate Protection, (iv) Modifying the Automatic Stay, and (v) Scheduling a Final Hearing, entered on May 6, 2016, or any final order referenced therein (collectively, the “DIP Financing”), unless such Event of Default was (a) caused by or related to any breach by MGF of the terms of this Agreement and/or the Sourcing Agreement, as modified by this Agreement; (b) cured by the Debtors in accordance with the terms of the DIP Financing or waived by the administrative agent under the DIP Financing within ten (10) calendar days of the occurrence of such Event of Default; or (c) caused by MGF’s acceleration of the Detailed Delivery Schedule (other than at the request of the Debtors)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c017",
    "name": "3. Trade Terms — Payment Method",
    "text": "All payments referenced herein shall be made by wire transfer of immediately available funds to the account designated by MGF in writing on or prior to the date hereof unless and until MGF changes such account designation in writing."
  },
  {
    "id": "c018",
    "name": "4. Run-Off License — Grant",
    "text": "4. Run-Off License. In the event of a liquidation of all or substantially all of the Debtors’ retail stores and/or the merchandise held for sale therein (a “Full Chain Liquidation”) approved by the Bankruptcy Court, beginning as of the commencement date of such Full Chain Liquidation as set forth in an agency agreement governing such Full Chain Liquidation (such date, the “Commencement Date”) and ending on the later of (x) December 31, 2017 and (y) one year after the commencement of such Full Chain Liquidation, the Debtors hereby grant MGF a worldwide, royalty-free, fully paid up, irrevocable run-off license to all of the Debtors’ trademarks and other intellectual property of any kind sufficient to permit MGF to sell Goods not yet delivered to the Debtors (but only to the extent that title to such Goods has not passed to the Debtors), subject to the following: (a) the run-off license shall not permit MGF (or its agents or representatives) to sell Goods in the United States during the sixty (60) day period immediately following the Commencement Date (it being agreed that in the event any such Full Chain Liquidation is stayed by the Bankruptcy Court for any reason, such sixty (60) day period shall be extended day-for-day concurrently with the period of such stay), and (b) if MGF wants to sell Goods to a third party in any country (other than the United States) in which the Debtors currently (as of the date hereof) authorize the sale of Aéropostale products to any licensee, then in such country MGF may only sell such Goods to such licensee."
  },
  {
    "id": "c019",
    "name": "4. Run-Off License — Permitted Uses",
    "text": "Subject to the foregoing limitations, the run-off license shall provide that, effective as of the commencement of such license as described above, MGF shall be entitled to complete the manufacture of, sell or otherwise dispose of all or any of the Goods not yet delivered to the Debtors (but only to the extent that title to such Goods has not passed to the Debtors) and make any advertisement or other promotion in furtherance thereof on a worldwide basis through one or more sales channels as MGF deems appropriate in it sole discretion (it being agreed and understood that no such advertisement or promotion shall be commenced until such run-off license becomes effective; for the avoidance of doubt, there shall be no advertising or promotion in the United States (or relating to sales of Goods to occur in the United States) prior to the date on which MGF is permitted to sell such Goods in the United States as set forth in clause (a) of the preceding sentence); provided that the run-off license shall be expressly limited to the foregoing and shall be valid for no other purpose."
  },
  {
    "id": "c020",
    "name": "4. Run-Off License — DIP Financing Exception",
    "text": "Notwithstanding the foregoing, MGF shall not be entitled to such license if the Court denies the proposed DIP Financing on a final basis based on the objection of Aero Investors LLC, MGF Sourcing Holdings, Limited (f/k/a TSAM Holdings, Limited) or Sycamore Partners or any of its affiliates."
  },
  {
    "id": "c021",
    "name": "5(a) MGF Release",
    "text": "5. Mutual Releases. (a) MGF, on behalf of itself and on behalf of any other person or entity that might claim by, through, or on behalf of MGF, including, as applicable, any past, present and future employees, agents, officers and directors of the foregoing (solely in their capacities as such, each a “MGF Releasor” and collectively, the “MGF Releasors”; it being acknowledged and agreed that in no event shall any affiliate of MGF be deemed to be a MGF Releasor), hereby generally releases, acquits and forever discharges the Debtors, and, as applicable, any past, present and future employees, agents, officers and directors of the foregoing (in each case solely in their capacities as such, each a “Debtor Releasee” and collectively, the “Debtor Releasees”), from any and all claims, crossclaims, counterclaims, disputes, demands, allegations, grievances, debts, liabilities, obligations, damages, losses, violations, actions, causes of action, suits, controversies, costs, charges and expenses (including attorneys’ fees and disbursements of counsel and other professionals), and requests for relief of every nature, kind, character or description 3 0652/21798-046 current/56348982v1 WEIL:\\95715512\\8\\11727.0013 16-11275-shl Doc 168 Filed 05/20/16 Entered 05/20/16 13:24:46 Main Document Pg 7 of 24 EXECUTION COPY whatsoever, whether prepetition or postpetition, at law or in equity, in contract or tort, known or unknown, foreseen or unforeseen, suspected or unsuspected, vested or unvested, absolute or contingent (collectively, “Claims”), which MGF or the MGF Releasors now have or ever had against the Debtors or one or more of the Debtor Releasees, except that this release will not release, impede, otherwise prevent or in any way affect (a) Claims arising out of the non-performance of any obligations set forth in this Settlement Agreement; (b) Claims by MGF or any MGF Releasor against any Debtor Releasee in any capacity other than as an employee, agent, officer and/or director of the Debtors; (c) the ability of MGF or any MGF Releasor to use any actions of the Debtors and/or the Debtor Releasees or facts underlying any released Claims hereunder in pursuing Claims against any Debtor Releasees in any capacity other than as employees, agents, officers and directors of the Debtors; and (d) any claim by MGF against the Debtors for any amounts owed to MGF for goods manufactured and delivered before the filing of bankruptcy but which remain unpaid (“Unpaid Pre-Petition Claims”)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c022",
    "name": "5(b) Debtors’ Release",
    "text": "(b) The Debtors, on behalf of themselves and on behalf of any other person or entity that might claim by, through, or on behalf of the Debtors, including, as applicable, any past, present and future employees, agents, officers and directors of the foregoing (solely in their capacities as such, each a “Debtor Releasor” and collectively, the “Debtor Releasors”), hereby generally releases, acquits and forever discharges MGF, and, as applicable, any past, present and future employees, agents, officers and directors of the foregoing (solely in their capacities as such, each a “MGF Releasee” and collectively, the “MGF Releasees”), from any and all Claims, which the Debtors or the Debtor Releasors now have or ever had against MGF or one or more of the MGF Releasees, except that this release will not release, impede, otherwise prevent or in any way affect (a) Claims arising out of the non-performance of any obligations set forth in this Settlement Agreement; (b) Claims by Debtors or any Debtor Releasor against any MGF Releasee in any capacity other than as an employee, agent, officer and/or director of MGF; (c) the ability of Debtors or any Debtor Releasor to use any actions of MGF and/or the MGF Releasees or facts underlying any released Claims hereunder in pursuing Claims against any MGF Releasees in any capacity other than as employees, agents, officers and directors of MGF; and (d) any defense (including, without limitation, defective product, non-conforming goods, shortages and similar defenses, but not based on delivery delays) by Debtors to any Unpaid Pre-Petition Claim."
  },
  {
    "id": "c023",
    "name": "5(c) Excluded Sycamore-Related Parties",
    "text": "(c) FOR THE AVOIDANCE OF DOUBT, THE GENERAL RELEASE WILL NOT EXTEND TO SYCAMORE PARTNERS, AERO INVESTORS LLC, MGF SOURCING HOLDINGS, LIMITED (f/k/a TSAM HOLDINGS, LIMITED), LEMUR LLC OR ANY OF THEIR AFFILIATES (OTHER THAN MGF) OR ANY OF THEIR EMPLOYEES, AGENTS, OFFICERS, OR DIRECTORS (ACTING IN SUCH CAPACITIES), EVEN FOR CONDUCT ARISING OUT OF OR RELATING TO THE RELEASED CONDUCT OF THE MGF RELEASEES."
  },
  {
    "id": "c024",
    "name": "5(d) Term Loan Obligations and Claims",
    "text": "(d) FOR THE AVOIDANCE OF DOUBT, THE GENERAL RELEASE WILL NOT AFFECT THE AMOUNT OF THE OBLIGATIONS UNDER THE LOAN AND SECURITY AGREEMENT, DATED MAY 23, 2014 (AS AMENDED, MODIFIED, OR 4 0652/21798-046 current/56348982v1 WEIL:\\95715512\\8\\11727.0013 16-11275-shl Doc 168 Filed 05/20/16 Entered 05/20/16 13:24:46 Main Document Pg 8 of 24 EXECUTION COPY OTHERWISE SUPPLEMENTED FROM TIME TO TIME) BY AND AMONG AЀROPOSTALE AS BORROWER, EACH DEBTOR-GUARANTOR NAMED THEREIN, THE VARIOUS FINANCIAL INSTITUTIONS AND OTHER PERSONS PARTY THERETO (THE “TERM LOAN LENDERS”) AND AERO INVESORS LLC AS ADMINSITRATIVE AGENT AND COLLATERAL AGENT, AND WILL NOT IMPEDE OR PREVENT OR AFFECT THE TERM LOAN LENDERS’ ABILITY TO PURSUE CLAIMS, IF ANY, AGAINST ANY OTHER PERSON OR ENTITY, INCLUDING THE DEBTORS, OR THE DEBTORS’ ABILITY TO DEFEND AGAINST SUCH CLAIMS."
  },
  {
    "id": "c025",
    "name": "5(e) California Civil Code Waiver",
    "text": "(e) Without limiting the foregoing, MGF and the Debtors hereby specifically waive the provisions of California Civil Code Section 1542, which provides as follows: “A GENERAL RELEASE DOES NOT EXTEND TO CLAIMS WHICH THE CREDITOR DOES NOT KNOW OR EXPECT TO EXIST IN HIS OR HER FAVOR AT THE TIME OF EXECUTING THE RELEASE, WHICH IF KNOWN TO HIM OR HER MUST HAVE MATERIALLY AFFECTED HIS OR HER SETTLEMENT WITH THE DEBTOR.”"
  },
  {
    "id": "c026",
    "name": "6. No New Debtor Orders",
    "text": "6. Sourcing Agreement Termination. The Debtors shall not submit any new orders to MGF under the Sourcing Agreement,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c027",
    "name": "6. Notice to International Licensees",
    "text": "and the Debtors shall notify their international licensees that they will not be permitted to submit any new orders to MGF."
  },
  {
    "id": "c028",
    "name": "6. Automatic Termination",
    "text": "After MGF makes the last delivery of Goods set forth on the Detailed Delivery Schedule and the Debtors make the final payment for Goods delivered by MGF, in each case as contemplated by this Agreement, the Sourcing Agreement shall automatically terminate and be of no further force or effect."
  },
  {
    "id": "c029",
    "name": "6. Termination Fees, Shortfall, and Rebates",
    "text": "The parties hereto each acknowledge and agree that the termination fee, the shortfall payment, and the rebate provisions of the Sourcing Agreement shall be of no further force or effect as of the date that the Settlement Order (as defined hereinafter) becomes a final order."
  },
  {
    "id": "c030",
    "name": "6. MGF Claim Waiver",
    "text": "MGF further agrees not to make any claim related to the termination fee and the shortfall payment under the Sourcing Agreement"
  },
  {
    "id": "c031",
    "name": "6. Debtors’ Rebate Waiver",
    "text": "and the Debtors agree to waive any claim for any rebate under the Sourcing Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c032",
    "name": "7. Interim Compliance",
    "text": "7. Bankruptcy Court Approval/Effectiveness of Agreement. The parties to this Agreement shall comply with the terms and conditions of this Agreement pending approval of this Agreement by the Bankruptcy Court,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c033",
    "name": "7. MGF Production and Delivery Obligations",
    "text": "and MGF shall continue to take all actions necessary to comply with its production and delivery obligations for all of the Goods."
  },
  {
    "id": "c034",
    "name": "7. Settlement Motion Filing and Approval",
    "text": "The Debtors shall file a revised version of Exhibit A to the motion to approve this Agreement pursuant to Rule 9019 of the Federal Rules of Bankruptcy Procedure (the “Settlement Motion”) on May 20, 2016, and shall seek the Settlement Motion’s approval by the Bankruptcy Court on May 23, 2016."
  },
  {
    "id": "c035",
    "name": "7. Failure of Court Approval",
    "text": "If the Debtors do not file the Settlement Motion and seek Bankruptcy Court approval thereof in accordance with the terms of this Agreement, or if the Bankruptcy Court either denies the Settlement Motion or fails to enter an order approving the Settlement Motion in form and substance reasonably acceptable to MGF (the “Settlement Order”) on or before May 30, 2016, then this Agreement shall be of no further force or effect;"
  },
  {
    "id": "c036",
    "name": "7. Surviving Payment Terms",
    "text": "provided that the Debtors’ obligation to pay for any Goods delivered prior thereto and MGF’s obligation to provide 14 day payment terms for any such Goods delivered prior thereto shall survive until fully performed."
  },
  {
    "id": "c037",
    "name": "8(a) MGF DIP Objection Withdrawal",
    "text": "EXECUTION COPY (a) DIP Financing Objection(s). Upon entry of the Settlement Order, MGF shall be deemed to have withdrawn its objection to the DIP Financing"
  },
  {
    "id": "c038",
    "name": "8(a) Cross Motions Withdrawal",
    "text": "and the Cross Motions shall each be deemed withdrawn."
  },
  {
    "id": "c039",
    "name": "8(a) Cross Motions Definition",
    "text": "“Cross Motions” means the Debtors’ Motion Pursuant to Sections 105(a), 362, and 365 of the Bankruptcy Code for Interim and Final Relief and to Compel Performance of MGF Sourcing US, LLC’s Obligations Under Executory Contract and to Enforce Automatic Stay (the “Debtors’ Motion to Compel”) and MGF’s Motion for an Order Under Sourcing Agreement §4(b)(ii), New York Uniform Commercial Code §§2-609 and 2-702 and 11 U.S.C. §105(a) (I) Compelling the Debtors to Pay Cash in Advance and Provide Letter of Credit Support Relating to Postpetition Deliveries of Goods; and (II) Authorizing Suspension of Performance under Sourcing Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c040",
    "name": "8(b) Discovery Stay",
    "text": "(b) Discovery. Pending the May 23, 2016 hearing on the Settlement Motion, discovery relating to the Debtors’ Motion to Compel shall be stayed."
  },
  {
    "id": "c041",
    "name": "8(b) Discovery Conference",
    "text": "The parties will continue to confer in good faith to discuss the scope and timing of discovery related to the Objection to the DIP Financing filed on behalf of Aero Investors LLC and MGF Holdings, Limited (f/k/a TSAM Holdings, Limited)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c042",
    "name": "8(c) Pricing Confidentiality",
    "text": "(c) Confidential Information. The parties acknowledge that the pricing information contained in the Detailed Delivery Schedule is confidential and proprietary information and they each agree to keep such pricing information confidential and not disclose it to any person or entity without the prior written consent of the other party."
  },
  {
    "id": "c043",
    "name": "8(c) Required Pricing Disclosures",
    "text": "If such pricing information is required to be disclosed under applicable law, regulation or legal process, or if necessary to enforce a party’s rights under this Agreement, the disclosing party must take all reasonable actions necessary to obtain a protective order or file the information under seal so as to protect the pricing information from disclosure, to the extent possible, consistent with the applicable law, regulation or legal process that made disclosure necessary."
  },
  {
    "id": "c044",
    "name": "8(c) Permitted Pricing Disclosures",
    "text": "Notwithstanding the foregoing, the Debtors may disclose the pricing information to the agent and lenders under the DIP Financing, the Debtors’ term loan lenders and, on a “professionals-eyes-only” basis, to the Official Committee of Unsecured Creditors appointed in the Debtors’ chapter 11 cases, in each case so long as the recipient agrees to keep such information confidential in accordance with this paragraph."
  },
  {
    "id": "c045",
    "name": "8(d) Delivery Cooperation",
    "text": "(d) Cooperation. The Debtors and MGF will reasonably cooperate with each other in the ordinary course with respect to delivery scheduling, timing and compliance with Debtors’ policies and procedures related to the delivery of goods (including with respect to MGF’s obligation to make delivery appointments with respect thereto), it being understood that the parties will coordinate through ordinary course business channels to manage situations such as significant deliveries falling on the same day and other minor delays due to scheduling and/or delivery issues that do not (i) in the case of the Debtors, materially impact their ability to deliver such goods to their retail stores in accordance with their existing production and warehousing delivery schedule and (ii) in the case of MGF, materially impact its ability to receive timely payment for such goods in accordance with the terms of section 3 (it being agreed that notwithstanding any provision herein or in the Sourcing Agreement to the contrary, the Debtors shall not be entitled to (A) charge back MGF for any such above described minor delays or (B) reject any deliveries as non-conforming deliveries unless any such late delivery is ten (10) days or more past the scheduled delivery date set forth on the Detailed Delivery Schedule)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c046",
    "name": "8(d) Assistance With Delivery or Acceptance",
    "text": "Without limiting the generality of the foregoing, to the extent that either the Debtors or MGF need assistance to comply with the delivery or acceptance of Goods, the other shall use reasonable business efforts, whenever possible, and the party seeking such assistance shall, whenever possible, provide the other party with reasonable advance notice of such need for assistance."
  },
  {
    "id": "c047",
    "name": "8(d) Delivery Schedule Discrepancies",
    "text": "The parties will continue to review the Detailed Delivery Schedule to identify any discrepancies (e.g., 6 0652/21798-046 current/56348982v1 WEIL:\\95715512\\8\\11727.0013 16-11275-shl Doc 168 Filed 05/20/16 Entered 05/20/16 13:24:46 Main Document Pg 10 of 24 EXECUTION COPY potential duplication of orders) and will cooperate in good faith to resolve any such discrepancies to eliminate any duplicate orders or other orders that the parties mutually agree (in writing) that MGF should not produce for the Debtors."
  },
  {
    "id": "c048",
    "name": "8(d) Public Announcements",
    "text": "Public announcements or public statements (including any commentary with respect to any of MGF and/or its affiliates and/or the Debtors) with respect to this Agreement or its terms and conditions shall be issued only with the mutual written consent of the Debtors and MGF."
  },
  {
    "id": "c049",
    "name": "8(e) Waiver",
    "text": "(e) Waiver. No waiver by either party of any breach by the other party of any condition or provision of this Agreement to be performed by such other party shall be deemed a waiver of any other provision or condition at the time or at any prior or subsequent time."
  },
  {
    "id": "c050",
    "name": "8(f) No Admission of Liability",
    "text": "(f) No Admission of Liability. It is understood that nothing in this Agreement is to be construed as an admission on behalf of the Debtors or MGF of any wrongdoing with respect to the Sourcing Agreement or otherwise, any such wrongdoing being expressly denied."
  },
  {
    "id": "c051",
    "name": "8(g) Entire Agreement",
    "text": "(g) Entire Agreement; Amendments; No Effect on DIP Financing. This Agreement, together with the Detailed Delivery Schedule and the Sourcing Agreement as modified hereby, shall constitute the entire agreement and understanding of the parties with respect to the subject matter herein and supersedes all prior agreements, arrangements and understandings, written or oral, between the parties with respect to the subject matter herein."
  },
  {
    "id": "c052",
    "name": "8(g) Adequate Consideration",
    "text": "Each party acknowledges and agrees that the consideration provided for in this Agreement is adequate consideration for the covenants and obligations of, and releases by, such party set forth in this Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c053",
    "name": "8(g) Amendments",
    "text": "Neither this Agreement nor the Sourcing Agreement may be altered, amended or modified except by a written instrument signed by the duly authorized officers or representatives of each party; provided that no such alteration, amendment or modification to any of the terms and conditions of either this Agreement or the Sourcing Agreement that is adverse to the interests of the lenders party to the DIP Financing shall be effective without the affirmative written consent of both any required lenders and the Agent under (and as defined in) the DIP Financing."
  },
  {
    "id": "c054",
    "name": "8(g) No Effect on DIP Financing",
    "text": "Nothing in this Agreement (or the Settlement Order entered by the Bankruptcy Court) shall be construed to alter or otherwise modify any of the terms or conditions of the DIP Financing and/or the orders of the Bankruptcy Court approving such DIP Financing."
  },
  {
    "id": "c055",
    "name": "8(g) Settlement Order Inclusion",
    "text": "The preceding sentence shall be expressly included in the Settlement Order."
  },
  {
    "id": "c056",
    "name": "8(h) Successors and Assigns",
    "text": "(h) Successors and Assigns. This Agreement is intended to bind and inure to the benefit of and be enforceable by the Debtors, MGF, and their respective successors and assigns."
  },
  {
    "id": "c057",
    "name": "8(h) Binding Effect on Purchasers and Successors",
    "text": "Without limiting the generality of the foregoing and notwithstanding anything to the contrary contained in this Agreement, the terms and conditions of this Agreement, including the releases granted in favor of MGF and the MGF Releasees, shall be binding on any purchaser of any of the Debtors’ assets or businesses, including as a going concern or in liquidation, any agent or other party granted the right to sell any of the Debtors’ inventory in store closing or similar themed sales, the reorganized Debtors, any subsequently appointed Chapter 11 or Chapter 7 trustee in the Debtors’ bankruptcy cases or any other successor to the Debtors."
  },
  {
    "id": "c058",
    "name": "8(h) Settlement Order Provision",
    "text": "The Settlement Order shall contain a provision to such effect."
  },
  {
    "id": "c059",
    "name": "8(i) Further Assurances",
    "text": "(i) Further Assurances. Each of the parties hereto agrees to do all things reasonably necessary, or as may be reasonably requested by other party, to carry out the purposes and intent of this Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c060",
    "name": "8(j) Counterparts",
    "text": "(j) Counterparts. This Agreement may be executed in one or more counterparts, each of which shall be deemed an original but all of which together shall constitute one and the same instrument."
  },
  {
    "id": "c061",
    "name": "8(k) Section Headings",
    "text": "(k) Section Headings; Construction. The headings of Sections in this Agreement are provided for convenience only and will not affect its construction or interpretation."
  },
  {
    "id": "c062",
    "name": "8(k) Section References",
    "text": "All references to “Section” or “Sections” refer to the corresponding Section or Sections of this Agreement unless otherwise specified."
  },
  {
    "id": "c063",
    "name": "8(k) Gender and Number Construction",
    "text": "All words used in this Agreement will be construed to be of such gender or number as the circumstances require."
  },
  {
    "id": "c064",
    "name": "8(k) Including Construction",
    "text": "Unless otherwise expressly provided, the word “including” does not limit the preceding words or terms."
  },
  {
    "id": "c065",
    "name": "8(l) Governing Law",
    "text": "(l) Governing Law. This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of New York, without regard to any applicable principles of conflicts of law of such or any other jurisdiction."
  },
  {
    "id": "c066",
    "name": "8(m) Continuing Effect of Sourcing Agreement",
    "text": "(m) Sourcing Agreement. Except as amended by this Agreement, the Sourcing Agreement remains in full force and effect until terminated in accordance with this Agreement."
  }
]

