     {"issue": "Automatic termination keyed to the last delivery and final payment cannot be squared with section 7, under which the entire Agreement becomes \"of no further force or effect\" if the Settlement Order is not entered by May 30, 2016, and with section 8(m)'s \"until terminated in accordance with this Agreement.\" What terminates the Sourcing Agreement if deliveries are never completed is left unresolved.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.23}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c029",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The termination fee, shortfall and rebate provisions die only when the Settlement Order \"becomes a final order,\" a term the Agreement never defines (non-appealable, or merely entered). Section 7 separately requires only entry of an approving order by May 30, leaving a gap in which those Sourcing Agreement provisions remain alive.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.22}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c030",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "MGF's unconditional agreement not to assert termination fee or shortfall claims sits against the preceding sentence, which extinguishes those Sourcing Agreement provisions only when the Settlement Order becomes a final order. Whether the waiver is likewise conditioned on finality can only be answered by reading the two together.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.17}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c031",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The Debtors' rebate waiver is stated unconditionally while the preceding sentence ties the death of the rebate provisions to the Settlement Order becoming a final order. A court could be asked whether the waiver survives a failure of finality under section 7.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.13}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c032",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The duty to comply \"pending approval\" of the Agreement cannot easily be squared with the last sentences of section 7, under which the Agreement becomes of no force if approval is denied and only the payment obligations survive. What becomes of performance rendered in the interim, and of the releases, is left to inference.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.20}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c033",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"all actions necessary to comply with its production and delivery obligations for all of the Goods\" sets an absolute standard with no force-majeure or practicability qualifier, in contrast to the \"where possible\" and \"to the extent practicable\" standards in sections 1(b) and 1(d). Which standard governs MGF's pre-approval performance is open.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.18}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c034",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The Debtors promise to \"seek the Settlement Motion's approval by the Bankruptcy Court on May 23, 2016,\" a date entirely within the court's control rather than the promisor's, with no standard for what counts as having sought approval. The obligation to file a \"revised version of Exhibit A\" also leaves the content of the revision unconstrained.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.16}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c035",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The Agreement fails unless an order is entered \"in form and substance reasonably acceptable to MGF,\" a subjective condition giving MGF latitude to declare an entered order unacceptable. Whether reasonableness is measured objectively, and who bears the burden, is not stated.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.33}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c036",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The survival proviso refers to \"MGF's obligation to provide 14 day payment terms,\" but section 3 casts the fourteen-day term as the Debtors' payment obligation, not an MGF obligation; the words mis-assign the duty. It also ignores section 3's cash-in-advance proviso, which may already have displaced fourteen-day terms.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.27}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c037",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"its objection to the DIP Financing\" does not identify which objection is withdrawn, and section 8(b) refers instead to an objection filed on behalf of Aero Investors LLC and MGF Holdings, Limited. Whether the affiliates' objection survives MGF's deemed withdrawal — which matters to the section 4 run-off license condition — is left open.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.24}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c038", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c039", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c040",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The discovery stay runs only \"pending the May 23, 2016 hearing,\" with no provision for an adjourned or continued hearing or for the period between hearing and ruling. If the hearing moves, the duration of the stay has no stated boundary.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.13}
   ]}
]}

